   "html_text": "Richard Posner (1978) also presents a critical account of privacy. He argues that from an economic perspective, we should not assign a property right to the personal information of individuals, when doing so leads to economic inefficiencies. This theoretical claim is linked to an empirical claim that common law follows a similar economic logic. Posner does not appear to deny that there is something that we can call “privacy” and a “right to privacy”. Instead, he argues that the notion of privacy",
   "md_text": "Richard Posner (1978) also presents a critical account of privacy. He argues that from an economic perspective, we should not assign a property right to the personal information of individuals, when doing so leads to economic inefficiencies. This theoretical claim is linked to an empirical claim that common law follows a similar economic logic. Posner does not appear to deny that there is something that we can call “privacy” and a “right to privacy”. Instead, he argues that the notion of privacy"
  },
